PRETABLE.out -- pvrrenderexit detector (draft probe39_draft_frozen.py, 39 rows), written BEFORE table 1 runs; its mtime is the order proof.
Fix under test: dev_pvr.c.fix (the round's working set, md5 481755b4f10f).  Design: cloud Fable 5.1's final ruling (adj_20261104/
FABLE_FINAL_r2.md, VERDICT GO-WITH-CHANGES, rows R1-R5).  R6-R8 are added here by the checks below; each is one cold session.

1. SIBLING PARITY.  The fix guards the depth store in TWO rasterizers, simpleline() and texturedline(); each is its own enclosing
   function with the same dominating predicates (x in range; vram_z[ofs] <= z) and the same new guard (!d->zwrite_disabled).  Parity
   means each rasterizer gets the same cells (section 3).  simpleline: ovoff, ovon, behind (R2, R3, R6).  texturedline: texoff,
   texbeh, texon (R4, and R7 = the two textured sessions this check adds).  Asymmetry before this check: Fable's rows gave simpleline
   three sessions and texturedline one (R4); the textured Z-on path and the textured Z-off-behind cell had no row.
   Sibling EXITS in the same function (texture pixel format :873, render mode :1090, list command :1431) are out of scope by the
   row's own state_note ("keep their own disposition"); the list-command exit was witnessed today (../sibling_listcmd_20261104/).

2. CLAIM -> ROW.  Every added comment sentence that asserts an observable consequence:
   a. field comment "When set, the rasterizers skip their vram_z stores" -> ovoff overlap, texoff overlap.
   b. field comment "Cleared at every pvr_render entry" and the reset's "a list with no header must not inherit the previous
      render's value" -> two overlap (R5).
   c. rasterizer comments "depth test kept, store skipped" -> kept: behind overlap, texbeh overlap (a Z-off polygon still FAILS the
      test behind a nearer one); skipped: ovoff and texoff overlap.
   d. case 4 comment "goes through the same depth test and rasterization as any other polygon" -> same depth test: behind and texbeh
      overlap (the fail side; R2 and R4 show only the pass side); rasterization: ovoff t1 only, texoff t1 only (drawn, not declined).
   e. "its depth values are not stored" -> ovoff and texoff overlap.  "Both rasterizers check d->zwrite_disabled" -> texoff, texbeh.
   f. "Before #NNN this bit ended the emulator with fatal() + exit(1)" -> the HEAD leg (zoff session and prompt red).
   No added sentence is left without a row.

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD.  The guard reads d->zwrite_disabled; the guarded body writes d->vram_z[ofs].  Writers of
   zwrite_disabled: DEVINIT's memset (0), the pvr_render entry (0), case 4 (= !zwrite).  Writers of vram_z: the render-entry clear
   (background z) and the two guarded stores.  States where the two disagree, each rowed: the field left at 1 by a previous render, at
   a render with no header (two, R5); the field set by one header and a later Z-on header in the same render (sticky, R8).
   PARTITION the body induces, per lvalue: zwrite_disabled tested zero / non-zero -> EXHAUSTED (both values rowed in each rasterizer);
   vram_z[ofs] <= z -> {pass, fail} -> EXHAUSTED per rasterizer; the EQUAL edge (vram_z == z) is NOT rowed: the comparator predates
   the fix and compares two variables, so rule D2 (a constant bound) does not bind -- disclosed under clause (e).
   JOINT CELLS {zwrite 0, 1} x {depth pass, fail}, per rasterizer:
     simpleline   (0,pass) ovon and behind t1   (0,fail) ovon overlap    (1,pass) ovoff t1, behind t2    (1,fail) behind overlap
     texturedline (0,pass) texbeh and texon t1  (0,fail) texon overlap   (1,pass) texoff t1, texbeh t2   (1,fail) texbeh overlap

4. CHANNEL -- per row, the variant it is written for and the observable that differs.  Rows no enumerated variant can move are
   CONTROLS by construction (they pin the channel: the frame clear, a Z-on triangle drawing, headerless vertices drawing).
   zoff session/prompt, and the session row of every Z-off session   B1_exit                exit 1, no prompt
   ovoff overlap                                                     M1, M3, M5, M7         0xf800 instead of 0x07e0
   ovoff t1 only, texoff t1 only                                     M11 (M12 simple only)  0x0000 instead of 0xf800
   ovon overlap                                                      M3, M6, M7, M15        0x07e0 instead of 0xf800
   behind overlap                                                    M13 (M3/M6/M7/M15 via T1)   0x07e0 instead of 0xf800
   behind t2 only, texbeh t2 only                                    M11 (M12 simple only)  0x0000 instead of 0x07e0
   texoff overlap                                                    M2, M4, M5, M7         0xf800 instead of 0x07e0
   texbeh overlap                                                    M14, M16, M4, M6, M7   0x07e0 instead of 0xf800
   texon overlap                                                     M4, M6, M7, M16        0x07e0 instead of 0xf800
   two overlap                                                       M9, M10                0x07e0 instead of 0xf800
   sticky overlap                                                    M8 (M3, M6, M7, M15)   0x001f instead of 0x07e0
   CONTROLS by this check (the draft's row() calls do not flag them yet; the probe is changed before landing, never during the table):
   zoff rendered, ovoff t2 only, ovoff bg, ovon t2 only, ovon t1 only, ovon bg, behind t1 only, texoff t2 only, texbeh t1 only,
   texon t2 only, two t1 only (R5's void condition: headerless vertices must draw), two t2 only, sticky t2 only -- beside the
   witness's six (neg apparatus, id session, id r8, zon session, zon rendered, zon prompt).
   CHANNEL, first mandated use, checked rather than obeyed: every detector row above names a variant under which its pixel MUST
   change, and the table measures whether it does; no detector row is survive-only at a refusal-effect site (the session rows are the
   clause-(b) channel, which an exit does move).

5. TABLE 1 -- the variants (variants/<name>.c, one exact edit each, written by pvr_variants.py) and the predicted red rows.
   B1_exit                  the removed `if (!zwrite) { fatal(...); exit(1); }`, verbatim, above the assignment
                            -> every Z-off session dies: 13/39 (= the HEAD leg's prediction)
   M1_simple_unguarded      simpleline store unconditional              -> ovoff overlap                               38/39
   M2_tex_unguarded         texturedline store unconditional            -> texoff overlap                              38/39
   M3_simple_inv            simpleline guard inverted                   -> ovoff, ovon, behind, two, sticky overlap    34/39
   M4_tex_inv               texturedline guard inverted                 -> texoff, texbeh, texon overlap               36/39
   M5_assign0               case 4: zwrite_disabled = 0                 -> ovoff, texoff overlap                       37/39
   M6_assign1               case 4: zwrite_disabled = 1                 -> ovon, behind, texbeh, texon, sticky overlap 34/39
   M7_assign_inv            case 4: zwrite_disabled = zwrite            -> ovoff, ovon, behind, texoff, texbeh, texon, sticky overlap 32/39
   M8_sticky                case 4: if (!zwrite) zwrite_disabled = 1    -> sticky overlap                              38/39
   M9_noreset               the entry reset deleted                     -> two overlap                                 38/39
   M10_reset_in_resetta     the reset moved into pvr_reset_ta()         -> two overlap (no session writes the TA reset) 38/39
   M11_decline              the draw dispatch skips Z-off polygons      -> ovoff t1, behind t2, texoff t1, texbeh t2   35/39
   M12_hoist_simple         simpleline: guard folded into the depth test, so Z-off polygons are not drawn -> ovoff t1, behind t2 37/39
   M13_ztest_bypass_simple  simpleline: <= z || zwrite_disabled         -> behind overlap                              38/39
   M14_ztest_bypass_tex     texturedline: the same                      -> texbeh overlap                              38/39
   M15_simple_never_store   simpleline guard && 0                       -> ovon, behind, two, sticky overlap           35/39
   M16_tex_never_store      texturedline guard && 0                     -> texbeh, texon overlap                       37/39
   M17_reset_at_end         the reset moved to the end of pvr_render    -> PREDICTED UNDETECTED (39/39), EQUIVALENT: the render
                            loop has no return or goto (grep, 2026-11-04), the field's only non-zero writer is inside that loop,
                            DEVINIT zeroes it, and the one early return (fb_base outside VRAM) precedes the loop -- so every render
                            begins with 0 either way.
   The scores above are PREDICTIONS; table 1's SCORES.txt is the record.  The HEAD leg is predicted 13/39 with SYMPTOM=PRESENT, and
   the three null media (/bin/true, an absent binary, /bin/false) CONTROL=FAIL.

6. ADDENDUM, 2026-11-04 17:1x, STILL BEFORE TABLE 1 RAN -- after Argon's design review (gweb jobs_20261103_adj/pvrrenderexit_det39,
   GWEBPVRDET: re-derived five predictions and found them right; named one gap).  THE GAP IS REAL AND IN-BOUND: both guarded stores sit
   under `if (x > 0 && x < d->xsize)`, a predicate DOMINATING the edited lines inside the enclosing function -- so DEPENDS-ON clause (1)
   enumerates it, and section 1 above named it ("x in range") without giving it a row.  Its two compares are relational against bounds
   (0, and xsize, 640 on this machine), so rule D2 pins each at its edges: one row per side, at most two per compare.  No earlier session
   drew within 10 pixels of either screen edge, so a one-token widening (x >= 0, x <= d->xsize: a store one column past a row's end,
   landing on the neighbouring row) went unobserved.
   ADDED (L1, pre-ship construction): two sessions, eight rows -- R9 `edges` (untextured) and `texedges` (textured, red texel), each a
   triangle across the LEFT edge (row 230 spans x = -30..30) and one across the RIGHT edge (row 330 spans x = 610..670):
     l in   (1, 230)   RED    column 1 drawn                 catches x > 1          (the tightening move of x > 0)
     l out  (0, 230)   BLACK  column 0 not drawn             catches x >= 0, and the bound deleted (x = 0 drawn)
     r in   (639, 330) RED    column 639 drawn               catches x < xsize - 1  (the tightening move of x < xsize)
     r out  (0, 331)   BLACK  x = 640 not wrapped onto 331   catches x <= xsize, and the bound deleted
   Odd pixel 1 and pixel 639 are read as the HIGH half of a 32-bit load at the even pixel below (little-endian).  The instrument is now
   probe47_draft_frozen.py (47 rows; 47/47 on build/gxemul, fixed_first47.out); probe39_draft_frozen.py stays as the record of the draft
   this file first described.  None of the eight new rows is a control.
   ADDED VARIANTS, each one token, each predicted to red exactly one row:
     M18_simple_lo_ge   x > 0 -> x >= 0             -> edges l out       46/47      M22_tex_lo_ge    the same in texturedline -> texedges l out
     M19_simple_lo_gt1  x > 0 -> x > 1              -> edges l in        46/47      M23_tex_lo_gt1   -> texedges l in
     M20_simple_hi_le   x < d->xsize -> <=          -> edges r out       46/47      M24_tex_hi_le    -> texedges r out
     M21_simple_hi_lt1  x < d->xsize -> < xsize - 1 -> edges r in        46/47      M25_tex_hi_lt1   -> texedges r in
   RESTATED DENOMINATORS: every section-5 prediction keeps its red set and gains the eight edge rows (green under all of M1-M17), so a
   prediction of k/39 becomes (k+8)/47; B1_exit and the HEAD leg become 21/47 (the edge sessions carry no Z-off header and survive).
   M17 stays PREDICTED UNDETECTED (47/47).  The three null media stay CONTROL=FAIL.

