   2 gaps).  Fable's stopped partial (DESIGN47_FABLE.md) is a seat failure, never a vote.
   a. AGREED by both and adopted: R6 behind, R7 texbeh, R8 sticky and R9 edges/texedges are OWED; the 26 predictions above stand (M10:
      pvr_reset_ta() runs only from DEVINIT and a PVRREG_RESET write, and the `two` session's render 2 reports 6 commands).
   b. THE GAP, named by both (Opus M26/M27, Mythos M29/M30): the depth compare's EQUAL edge.  `vram_z[ofs] <= z` -> `< z` changes no pixel
      of the 47 rows, because no session draws two polygons at one z.  Section 3 excluded it as "two variables, so D2 does not bind"; both
      seats rejected that reading (the ruling's D2 carries no constant-bound limit, and M19/M21 already treat a tightening of
      `x < d->xsize`, also two variables, as in bound).  ADDED (L1, pre-ship construction): R10, sessions `equal` (untextured) and
      `texequal` (red and green texels), each a Z-on T1 at z = 2.0 then a Z-on T2 at z = 2.0 over it:
        equal overlap      (220,180) GREEN  ties go to the later polygon under <=    catches M29
        equal t2 only      (320,180) GREEN  T2 drawn                                 CONTROL
        texequal overlap   (220,180) GREEN  the same in texturedline                 catches M30
        texequal t2 only   (320,180) GREEN  T2 drawn from its texel                  CONTROL
      REACHABILITY, read before any run: three vertices at z = 2.0 give dz12 = dz13 = dz23 = 0.0 in pvr_render_triangle and dz12 = 0 in
      simpleline, so z is exactly 2.0 at every pixel (texturedline likewise).  The legs' base run settles it: if `equal overlap` reads
      0xf800 on the fix, the edge is unreachable on this tree and R10 is recorded VOID beside this addendum, never rewritten.
   c. THE DISAGREEMENT, texon.  Opus: EXCESS, "its red set {M4, M6, M7, M16} is entirely inside texbeh overlap's red set".  Mythos: OWED, by
      the joint cell {zwrite 0, depth fail} in texturedline, and it names the in-bound variant only texon sees, M27: texturedline
      `<= z || !d->zwrite_disabled` (a Z-on polygon skips the depth test); texbeh's T2 is Z-off, so the test still applies there.
      Re-derived here: M27 leaves texoff, texbeh, texedges and texequal green and reds texon overlap alone.  DECIDED NOW, SETTLED BY
      TABLE 1: if M27's red set is exactly {texon overlap}, texon is OWED and stays; if any other row reds under M27, texon is excess and
      is dropped before landing.
   d. THE CONTROLS, section 4 CORRECTED.  Opus is right and section 4 was wrong: eight of its thirteen "controls" sit in Z-off sessions,
